<article class="env-example" id="ACAD57">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/ACAD57">Example <span data-tag="ACAD57">8.2.9.31</span>.</a> If ${\mathbf A}$ is the category of simplicial sets, then the map $\gamma $ of Corollary <a href="/tag/44602B" data-tag="44602B">8.2.9.30</a> is always an isomorphism; this follows from Example <a href="/tag/F9111E" data-tag="F9111E">8.2.9.21</a>. In other words, if $X_{\bullet , \bullet }$ is a bisimplicial set, then we can identify the diagonal simplicial set $[n] \mapsto X_{n,n}$ with the homotopy colimit of corresponding diagram $\cDelta ^{op} \rightarrow \sSet $. </p>
</article>